message.content:
{
  "message": "Thanks for the detailed provider contract (v2). I've mapped Spokes' order data to your shipment API and identified several mismatches that need decisions or conversions. Key gaps: phone format (UK free-text → +447XXXXXXXXX), address parsing (single line → structured fields), postcode normalization (as-is → uppercase + space), weight conversion (kg→g), parcel size tier mapping (kg→A/B/C), parcel vs pallet routing (>25kg), postcode-city validation, idempotency key mapping (ORD-XXXX), reference mapping (ORD-XXXX), status mapping (CREATED/COLLECTED/IN_TRANSIT/DELIVERED/RETURNED/CANCELLED → pending/paid/shipped/delivered/cancelled), and webhook signature verification. I've added semantic mappings for the mechanical conversions, consumer decisions for the mechanical mappings, consumer scenarios for Spokes' real edge cases (phone formats, address parsing, heavy cargo bikes, idempotent payment retries, webhook handling), and two end-to-end scenarios covering paid→shipped→delivered and a heavy cargo bike that must go pallet. I have two business questions for the Spokes product owner about status mapping for RETURNED and whether to auto-create shipments on payment or keep manual warehouse flow.",
  "patches": [
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/semantic_mappings",
      "value": {
        "phone_to_e164": {
          "from": "UK free-text (e.g. '07700 900200', '+44 7700 900200', '0044 7700-900200', '(+44) 7700-900200', '447700900200')",
          "to": "+447XXXXXXXXX (E.164, exactly 13 chars: +447 + 9 digits)"
        },
        "address_line_to_structured": {
          "from": "Single free-text line, UK format with postcode last (e.g. 'Behind the old mill, London SW1A 1AA' or '10 Example Rd, E1 6AN')",
          "to": "{street, building, postcode, city, country: 'GB'}"
        },
        "postcode_normalize": {
          "from": "As typed (may be lowercase, missing space, extra spaces)",
          "to": "Uppercase, exactly one space, regex ^[A-Z]{1,2}\\d[A-Z\\d]? \\d[A-Z]{2}$"
        },
        "weight_kg_to_g": {
          "from": "Float kg with 3 decimals (e.g. 0.3, 14.5, 27.0)",
          "to": "Integer grams (weight_kg * 1000, rounded)"
        },
        "weight_g_to_size_tier": {
          "from": "Integer grams",
          "to": "A (<=5000), B (5001-15000), C (15001-25000)"
        },
