{
  "message": "I've analyzed the mismatches between Spokes (consumer) and Parcelly (provider). Key mismatches: phone format normalization, address parsing, weight conversion (kg→g) with parcel/pallet tier selection, postcode normalization & city matching, idempotency key strategy, order↔shipment status mapping, webhook signature verification, and order-paid→shipment-creation flow. I have 2 business questions for you.",
  "patches": [
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/decisions/-",
      "value": {
        "id": "C1",
        "title": "Phone number normalization to E.164 +447XXXXXXXXX",
        "rule": "Consumer normalizes all UK phone formats (07700 900200, 07700900200, +447700900200, +44 7700 900234, 0044 7700-900200, (+44) 7700-900345, 447700900567, 07700-900890) to E.164 +447XXXXXXXXX before sending to provider. Provider validates and returns 422 INVALID_PHONE on mismatch.",
        "owner": "consumer",
        "source": "app/services/orders.py, docs/INTERNAL.md",
        "public": true
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/decisions/-",
      "value": {
        "id": "C2",
        "title": "Free-text address_line parsing into structured address",
        "rule": "Consumer parses free-text address_line (postcode last after city, UK format, possibly incomplete e.g. 'Behind the old mill, London') into structured fields: street, building, postcode, city, country=GB. Postcode normalized to uppercase with single space. Provider validates postcode format and postcode-city match, returns 422 INVALID_POSTCODE or 422 POSTCODE_CITY_MISMATCH.",
        "owner": "consumer",
        "source": "docs/INTERNAL.md",
        "public": true
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/decisions/-",
      "value": {
        "id": "C3",
        "title": "Weight conversion (kg→g) and parcel vs pallet selection with size tier",
        "rule": "Consumer converts order weight_kg (float, 3 decimals, sum of unit_weight_kg * quantity) to weight_g (int grams). If weight_g ≤ 25000: use create_shipment with parcel size tier A (≤5000g), B (5001-15000g), C (15001-25000g) matching weight. If weight_g > 25000: use create_pallet (25001-1000000g). Cargo bikes >25kg (27kg, 31.5kg) go to pallet. Provider validates weight-tier match (422 SIZE_WEIGHT_MISMATCH) and pallet weight range (422 PALLET_WEIGHT_OUT_OF_RANGE).",
        "owner": "consumer",
        "source": "app/services/orders.py, docs/INTERNAL.md",
        "public": true
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/decisions/-",
      "value": {
        "id": "C4",
        "title": "Postcode-city mismatch handling",
        "rule": "Provider validates postcode area (e.g. SW from SW1A 1AA) matches city and returns 422 POSTCODE_CITY_MISMATCH. Consumer relies on provider validation and handles 422 error; no client-side pre-validation required.",
        "owner": "consumer",
        "origin_question": "Q2",
        "public": true
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/decisions/-",
      "value": {
        "id": "C5",
        "title": "Idempotency-Key strategy for create_shipment/create_pallet",
        "rule": "Consumer always sends Idempotency-Key header using order_id (format ORD-XXXX) for create_shipment and create_pallet. Key ≤255 chars. Provider treats missing/blank key as new shipment each time; consumer uses key for idempotent retries.",
        "owner": "consumer",
        "origin_question": "Q1",
        "public": true
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/decisions/-",
      "value": {
        "id": "C6",
        "title": "Order status to shipment status mapping for webhook handling",
        "rule": "Consumer maps Parcelly shipment.status_changed webhook events to internal order status: CREATED→pending (order created), COLLECTED→shipped, IN_TRANSIT→shipped, DELIVERED→delivered, RETURNED→cancelled (with support note). Webhook handlers are idempotent (provider retries 5× with backoff). Order paid handlers trigger shipment creation.",
        "owner": "consumer",
        "source": "app/services/order_events.py, docs/INTERNAL.md",
        "public": true
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/decisions/-",
      "value": {
        "id": "C7",
        "title": "Webhook signature verification (HMAC-SHA256)",
        "rule": "Consumer verifies Parcelly webhook signature: computes HMAC-SHA256 of raw request body using webhook_secret (from webhook registration), compares to X-Parcelly-Signature header (sha256=<hex>). Returns 200 for valid, 401 for invalid/missing. Provider retries 5× (0.5s, 1s, 2s, 4s, 8s); any 2xx = success.",
        "owner": "consumer",
        "source": "provider API spec",
        "public": true
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/decisions/-",
      "value": {
        "id": "C8",
        "title": "Order paid → shipment creation integration",
        "rule": "When order status changes from pending to paid (via POST /orders/{id}/pay or payment gateway callback), ORDER_PAID_HANDLERS run. Consumer adds handler that: (1) computes total weight_g from order items, (2) selects create_shipment (parcel) or create_pallet based on weight, (3) builds receiver from order customer_name, phone, address_line, (4) sends create_shipment/create_pallet with Idempotency-Key=order_id, (5) stores returned shipment_id/tracking_number on order. Handler is idempotent (payment gateway may retry).",
        "owner": "consumer",
        "source": "app/services/order_events.py, app/services/orders.py",
        "public": true
      }
    }
  ],
  "questions_for_human": [
    {
      "text": "Idempotency-Key strategy: Provider defaults to optional (missing/blank = new shipment each time). Consumer decides whether to always send it. Decision C5 proposes always sending order_id as Idempotency-Key. Confirm this is your intent, or should consumer sometimes omit it?",
      "options": [
        "Always send Idempotency-Key=order_id (consumer owns idempotency)",
        "Send only for retries (first attempt without key)",
        "Never send (accept duplicate charges on retry)"
      ],
      "default": "Always send Idempotency-Key=order_id (consumer owns idempotency)"
    },
    {
      "text": "Postcode-city mismatch: Provider validates and returns 422 POSTCODE_CITY_MISMATCH. Decision C4 says consumer relies on provider validation. Confirm, or should consumer pre-validate using a postcode lookup service?",
      "options": [
        "Rely on provider 422 error (consumer handles error)",
        "Pre-validate client-side with postcode API",
        "Pre-validate with embedded postcode-city database"
      ],
      "default": "Rely on provider 422 error (consumer handles error)"
    }
  ],
  "status": "continue"
}

