  "message": "Adding Spokes integration decisions (D3–D12), consumer scenarios (S1–S4), and e2e scenarios (E2–E3). Two questions for Parcelly remain open.\n\n**Decisions added** (fit Parcelly's API v6):\n- D3: Address mapping – parse UK postcode from end of free-text address_line, uppercase, validate regex ^[A-Z]{1,2}\\d[A-Z\\d]? \\d[A-Z]{2}$, derive city from outward code via lookup, remainder → street/building. Mismatch → block per H1.\n- D4: Phone normalization – strip non-digits, ensure starts with 447, prepend '+', validate ^\\+447\\d{9}$ (13 chars). Invalid → block shipment, flag support.\n- D5: Weight – Spokes weight_kg (float, 3dp) → weight_g = round(weight_kg * 1000). ≤25,000g → parcel; >25,000g → pallet (H2).\n- D6: Parcel size tier – auto-map weight_g: A ≤5,000g, B 5,001–15,000g, C 15,001–25,000g. Mismatch → 422 SIZE_WEIGHT_MISMATCH.\n- D7: Status mapping – Spokes paid → create shipment (CREATED); warehouse marks shipped → COLLECTED; carrier collects → IN_TRANSIT; delivered → DELIVERED. Cancelled → no shipment. Webhook shipment.status_changed → Spokes status idempotently.\n- D8: Idempotency-Key – use Spokes order_id (e.g. ORD-1001) as Idempotency-Key header (≤255 chars, per-partner scope). 4xx → key not stored, retry after fix.\n- D9: Postcode/city validation – maintain UK outward-code → city lookup; mismatch → 422 POSTCODE_CITY_MISMATCH → block per H1.\n- D10: Pallet shipments – cargo bikes (>25kg) → pallet_type EUR, weight_g 25,001–1,000,000g. Pricing from Parcelly sandbox (Q3).\n- D11: Webhook handling – register at setup, verify HMAC-SHA256, retry 5× (0.5s,1s,2s,4s,8s), map status idempotently.\n- D12: Sandbox – use Parcelly sandbox endpoints (/__sandbox/partners, /__sandbox/reset, /__sandbox/shipments/{id}/advance) in test suite.\n\n**Questions for Parcelly:**\n- Q3: Exact pallet pricing formula in sandbox? (Needed for D10 test scenarios.)\n- Q4: Does sandbox webhook endpoint /__sandbox/webhook exist for testing delivery retries, or should we use a local test server?",
