{
  "message": "I've analyzed the current contract (v9) and identified several concrete issues the consumer (Spokes) can fix:\n\n1. **Duplicate decisions**: D14-D21, H3, H4 appear twice in the decisions array\n2. **Incorrect semantic mappings**: The mappings include `in_transit` (not a Spokes status per INTERNAL.md) and miss `pending`/`cancelled` mappings per the order lifecycle (pending→paid→shipped→delivered, cancelled from pending)\n3. **E2E scenarios E1/E2 contradict H4**: They expect automatic order status update to 'delivered' on webhook, but H4 (consumer decision) states warehouse manually confirms delivery\n4. **E1 uses invalid provider status**: Uses `SHIPPED` (not a Parcelly status) instead of `COLLECTED`\n5. **Consumer scenario coverage refs are wrong**: S1 cites D15 (address parsing) but tests phone normalization (D12); S2 cites D16 (weight conversion) but tests incomplete address (D20)\n6. **Missing consumer decisions** for key integration rules: payment handler idempotency, order-paid triggers shipment creation, order lifecycle mapping\n7. **Missing consumer scenarios** for order-paid→shipment flow and webhook handling with manual delivery confirmation",
  "patches": [
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/decisions",
      "value": [
        { "id": "D1", "title": "Parcel size must match weight_g: A (1-5000g), B (5001-15000g), C (15001-25000g). Mismatch returns 422 SIZE_WEIGHT_MISMATCH.", "side": "provider", "origin_question": null },
        { "id": "D2", "title": "Pallet weight_g must be 25001-1000000g. Outside range returns 422 PALLET_WEIGHT_OUT_OF_RANGE.", "side": "provider", "origin_question": null },
        { "id": "D3", "title": "Postcode area (first 1-2 letters) must match receiver.address.city. Mismatch returns 422 POSTCODE_CITY_MISMATCH.", "side": "provider", "origin_question": null },
        { "id": "D4", "title": "Idempotency-Key longer than 255 characters returns 400 INVALID_IDEMPOTENCY_KEY. Blank or missing key creates a new shipment each time.", "side": "provider", "origin_question": null },
        { "id": "D5", "title": "Webhook shipment.status_changed emitted only on genuine status transitions (CREATED→COLLECTED, COLLECTED→IN_TRANSIT, IN_TRANSIT→DELIVERED, IN_TRANSIT→RETURNED). Creating a shipment (status CREATED) does NOT emit a webhook. Re-setting the same status does NOT emit a webhook.", "side": "provider", "origin_question": null },
        { "id": "D6", "title": "Tracking numbers follow format PCL<n>GB for parcel service and PAL<n>GB for pallet service.", "side": "provider", "origin_question": null },
        { "id": "D7", "title": "Parcel pricing: size A = 1299 pence, B = 1599 pence, C = 1999 pence. Pallet pricing: EUR pallet = 8900 pence. Price returned in price_pence field.", "side": "provider", "origin_question": null },
        { "id": "D8", "title": "Receiver phone must match ^\\+447\\d{9}$ (UK mobile E.164). Invalid format returns 422 INVALID_PHONE.", "side": "provider", "origin_question": null },
        { "id": "D9", "title": "Receiver address postcode must match ^[A-Z]{1,2}\\d[A-Z\\d]? \\d[A-Z]{2}$ (uppercase, exactly one space). Invalid format returns 422 INVALID_POSTCODE.", "side": "provider", "origin_question": null },
        { "id": "D10", "title": "Receiver address country must be GB. Any other value returns 400 INVALID_REQUEST.", "side": "provider", "origin_question": null },
        { "id": "D11", "title": "Parcelly sends X-Parcelly-Signature: sha256=<hex> computed as HMAC-SHA256(raw_body, webhook_secret). Consumer verifies signature over exact raw request bytes before processing. Invalid signature → return 401.", "side": "provider", "origin_question": null },
        { "id": "D12", "title": "Idempotency keys are scoped to partner. A 4xx response does not store the key, allowing corrected retry with same key.", "side": "provider", "origin_question": null },
        { "id": "D13", "title": "Reference field max length 64 characters. Receiver name max 120. Address street max 120, building max 20, flat max 20, city max 80.", "side": "provider", "origin_question": null },
        { "id": "H1", "title": "For cargo bikes >25kg (e.g., Spokes Haul 2 at 27kg/31.5kg): should we use Parcelly's pallet endpoint, or exclude these orders from automated shipping and handle manually? Answer: Use pallet endpoint for >25kg orders", "side": "consumer", "origin_question": "Q1" },
        { "id": "H2", "title": "For incomplete addresses (e.g., 'Behind the old mill, London' with no clear postcode): should shipment creation fail fast with validation error, or queue for manual review by warehouse team? Answer: Fail shipment creation (return error to order paid handler)", "side": "consumer", "origin_question": "Q2" },
        { "id": "D14", "title": "Spokes stores UK phone numbers in free-text format. Parcelly requires E.164 +447XXXXXXXXX. Consumer normalizes by stripping non-digits, ensuring leading +447, and validating 11 digits after +44.", "side": "consumer", "origin_question": null },
        { "id": "D15", "title": "Spokes stores address as single free-text line. Parcelly requires structured fields: street, building, postcode, city, country=GB. Consumer extracts postcode (UK format, last token), city (token before postcode), street+building from remainder. If postcode/city cannot be extracted, fail fast.", "side": "consumer", "origin_question": null },
        { "id": "D16", "title": "Spokes stores weight_kg as float. Parcelly requires weight_g integer (grams). Consumer converts: weight_g = round(weight_kg * 1000). Parcel threshold: weight_g ≤ 25000 → parcel (size A/B/C by weight tier); weight_g > 25000 → pallet endpoint. Cargo bikes >25kg use pallet endpoint.", "side": "consumer", "origin_question": null },
        { "id": "D17", "title": "Parcel size tier derived from weight_g: A ≤ 5000g, B 5001-15000g, C 15001-25000g. Consumer selects size field accordingly.", "side": "consumer", "origin_question": null },
        { "id": "D18", "title": "Spokes uses handler-based idempotency. Parcelly uses Idempotency-Key header (≤255 chars, scoped per partner). Consumer sends Spokes order reference as Idempotency-Key on shipment creation.", "side": "consumer", "origin_question": null },
        { "id": "D19", "title": "Parcelly sends X-Parcelly-Signature: sha256=<hex> computed as HMAC-SHA256(raw_body, webhook_secret). Consumer verifies signature over exact raw request bytes before processing. Invalid signature → return 401.", "side": "consumer", "origin_question": null },
        { "id": "D20", "title": "For incomplete addresses (e.g., 'Behind the old mill, London' with no clear postcode), shipment creation fails fast with validation error returned to order paid handler.", "side": "consumer", "origin_question": null },
        { "id": "D21", "title": "For cargo bikes >25kg (e.g., Spokes Haul 2 at 27kg/31.5kg), consumer uses Parcelly's pallet endpoint.", "side": "consumer", "origin_question": null },
        { "id": "H3", "title": "For orders with multiple items shipping to different addresses (split shipments): should Spokes create one Parcelly shipment per address, or is this not supported in current order model? Answer: Not supported - single address per order", "side": "consumer", "origin_question": "Q3" },
        { "id": "H4", "title": "When Parcelly webhook delivers 'delivered' status, should Spokes automatically mark order as 'delivered', or does warehouse team still manually confirm? Answer: Warehouse manually confirms", "side": "consumer", "origin_question": "Q4" },
        { "id": "D22", "title": "Order paid event handlers (ORDER_PAID_HANDLERS) must be idempotent: payment gateway may retry confirmations (second call finds order already paid, keeps original paid_at, calls handlers again). Exception in a handler is logged and does not undo payment; remaining handlers still run.", "side": "consumer", "origin_question": null },
        { "id": "D23", "title": "When order status changes from pending to paid, Spokes creates a Parcelly shipment (parcel or pallet based on weight_g). This happens in an ORDER_PAID_HANDLER and must be idempotent (uses order reference as Idempotency-Key).", "side": "consumer", "origin_question": null },
        { "id": "D24", "title": "Spokes order status lifecycle: pending → paid → shipped → delivered, with cancelled as a branch from pending via support. No automated carrier status; shipped and delivered set manually by warehouse team.", "side": "consumer", "origin_question": null },
        { "id": "D25", "title": "POST /orders/{id}/pay returns 409 ORDER_NOT_PAYABLE if order status not in (pending, paid). Duplicate payment confirmation does not change paid_at; original timestamp preserved.", "side": "consumer", "origin_question": null }
      ]
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/semantic_mappings/spokes_order_status_to_shipment_status",
      "value": {
        "paid": "CREATED",
        "shipped": "COLLECTED",
        "delivered": "DELIVERED",
        "cancelled": "RETURNED"
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/semantic_mappings/shipment_status_to_spokes_order_status",
      "value": {
        "CREATED": "paid",
        "COLLECTED": "shipped",
        "IN_TRANSIT": "shipped",
        "DELIVERED": "delivered",
        "RETURNED": "cancelled"
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "replace",
      "path": "/scenarios/0",
      "value": {
        "id": "E1",
        "title": "Paid order triggers parcel shipment; warehouse marks shipped, delivery webhook updates to delivered pending manual confirmation",
        "side": "e2e",
        "covers": [
          "create_shipment",
          "shipment_status_changed"
        ],
        "steps": [
          {
            "do": {
              "party": "provider",
              "action": "reset"
            }
          },
          {
            "do": {
              "party": "consumer",
              "action": "reset"
            }
          },
          {
            "do": {
              "party": "consumer",
              "action": "create_order",
              "args": {
                "title": "Sea Tales",
                "pages": 120
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "do": {
              "party": "consumer",
              "action": "pay_order"
            }
          },
          {
            "send": {
              "operation": "create_shipment",
              "headers": {
                "Authorization": "Bearer {{ctx.api_key}}",
                "Idempotency-Key": "{{ctx.order_ref}}"
              },
              "body": {
                "reference": "{{ctx.order_ref}}",
                "receiver": {
                  "name": "John Smith",
                  "phone": "+447700900200",
                  "address": {
                    "street": "Baker Street",
                    "building": "22",
