We need to see why duplicate API key returns 201 instead of 409. Likely because the sandbox endpoint uses the partner registry but maybe the create function doesn't throw? Let's look at sandbox.js line where create partner is handled.

In sandbox.js we saw:

router.post("/partners", (request, response) => {
  validateSandboxPartner(request.body);
  const { name, api_key, flags } = request.body;
  let partner = partners.findByApiKey(api_key);
  if (!partner) {
    partner = partners.create({ name, apiKey: api_key, flags });
  }
  response.status(201).json({ partner_id: partner.id, api_key: partner.apiKey });
});

It checks if partner exists; if not, creates; else returns existing partner with 201 (should be 409). According to test, they expect conflict on duplicate API key. So we need to change to return 409 when partner exists.

Thus edit sandbox.js to throw ApiError 409 API_KEY_TAKEN when partner exists.

